{"name":"Under the Sun","hex":"#efd100","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"under the sun","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Prepositional phrase","definitions":["In existence."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/under_the_sun"}],"entries":[{"title":"Under the Sun (1998 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Under the Sun is a Swedish film which was released to cinemas in Sweden on 25 December 1998, directed by Colin Nutley, adapted from the short story The Little Farm by H. E. Bates. The film stars Rolf Lassgård, Helena Bergström, and Johan Widerberg. Set in Sweden in the mid-1950s, the film was nominated for the 1999 Academy Award for Best Foreign Language Film."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/80/Under_the_Sun_%28film%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Under_the_Sun_(1998_film)","wikidata":"Q1169261"},{"title":"Under the Sun (2015 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Under the Sun is a 2015 documentary film directed by Vitaly Mansky. It depicts a year in the life of a family in Pyongyang, North Korea, as their daughter, Zin-mi, prepares to join the Korean Children's Union on the Day of the Shining Star."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/c2/Under_the_Sun_%282015_film%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Under_the_Sun_(2015_film)","wikidata":"Q22570084"},{"title":"Under the Sun (Cheryl song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Under the Sun\" is a song recorded by English singer Cheryl, from her third studio album A Million Lights (2012). The song was released as the second and final single from A Million Lights on 2 September 2012 through Fascination Records. It was written and produced by Alex da Kid, with additional writing from Mike Del Rio, Jayson DeZuzio, Steven Battey, Carlos Battey, and Cheryl. Lyrically, it speaks of a male telling a female anything she wants to hear to get his way. \"Under the Sun\" is a mid-tempo song with piano riffs, sun-kissed breakbeats, and a pop chorus."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/83/Cheryl_-_Under_the_Sun_%28Official_Single_Cover%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Under_the_Sun_(Cheryl_song)","wikidata":"Q4004585"},{"title":"Sun","blocks":[{"text":"The Sun is the star located at the centre of the Solar System. It is a massive sphere of hot plasma, heated to incandescence by nuclear fusion reactions in its core, radiating the energy from its surface mainly as visible light and infrared radiation, with 10% at ultraviolet energies. It is the main source of energy for life on Earth. The Sun has been an object of veneration in many cultures and a central subject of astronomical research since antiquity."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/The_Sun_in_white_light.jpg/330px-The_Sun_in_white_light.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sun","wikidata":"Q525"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/Vitaly_Mansky_2014_Pyongyang%2C_North_Korea.jpg/500px-Vitaly_Mansky_2014_Pyongyang%2C_North_Korea.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/Vitaly_Mansky_2014_Pyongyang%2C_North_Korea.jpg/1280px-Vitaly_Mansky_2014_Pyongyang%2C_North_Korea.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/Vitaly_Mansky_2014_Pyongyang%2C_North_Korea.jpg/500px-Vitaly_Mansky_2014_Pyongyang%2C_North_Korea.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Mansky at the Mansu Hill Grand Monument in Pyongyang in 2014","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AVi